<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="timeline">
    <h2>The Road to the Reveal — Project Camelot Timeline</h2>
    <p>All evidence was not equal. This is what had actually been observed versus what remained theory leading into BlizzCon, and how the community tracked a product Blizzard never fully named until the show.</p>
    <h3>Observed — datamined & tracked</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Project Camelot naming in Blizzard's backend information</li>
        <li>An encrypted WoW 1.60 development branch, with 29+ encrypted builds logged on the branch since October 2025</li>
        <li>Heroic and Epic licensing references</li>
        <li>Updates across multiple development environments</li>
        <li>Brief appearances on Blizzard vendor environments — Western and Chinese</li>
        <li>Development advancing to Patch 1.60.1</li>
        <li>Encrypted promotional assets under investigation</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Interpretation — what the activity may indicate</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>Camelot received continued development right up to the show (wowdev2 hit 1.60.1.69800 over reveal weekend)</li>
        <li>Blizzard maintained more than one test branch</li>
        <li>The project always involved a substantial WoW product</li>
        <li>Some development activity related to Classic infrastructure</li>
    </ul>
    <ul class="news-list">
        <li><time>Oct 2025</time> Encrypted WoW 1.60 activity begins appearing on Blizzard's internal infrastructure.</li>
        <li><time>Jan 29 2026</time> Executive producer Holly Longdale begins announcing what's next for Classic during State of Azeroth before a staged power outage cuts her off mid-sentence ("I guess we'll save that for later"). Blizzard later confirms the cutoff was intentional.</li>
        <li><time>Jun 16 2026</time> "World of Warcraft: Camelot" references go public alongside Heroic and Epic licensing labels.</li>
        <li><time>Jul 29 2026</time> Possible Alliance and Horde Lordaeron tabard textures raise questions about Camelot's setting.</li>
        <li><time>Late Jul 2026</time> The encrypted 1.60 build briefly appears on a Blizzard vendor environment before returning to internal development.</li>
        <li><time>Jul 31 2026</time> An identical 1.60.0 build appears across additional internal environments, indicating broader internal distribution.</li>
        <li><time>Aug 7 2026</time> wowdev2 advances from 1.60.0 to 1.60.1 — the first detected point-one branch.</li>
        <li><time>Aug 14-15 2026</time> wowdev5 and wowdev2 receive new builds while encrypted Dwarf and Skyborne promotional rewards add more theories — Stiven suggests the Dev Five line may be stabilized for a BlizzCon playable demo.</li>
        <li><time>Aug 18 2026</time> An anonymous forum post claims an October 13 release with neutral Dalaran, a battle pass and new races — unconfirmed rumor, not datamined or official.</li>
        <li><time>Aug 20 2026</time> Project Camelot's encrypted build appears on China's vendor server. NetEase had committed over a year earlier to launching Classic+ simultaneously for Chinese and Western audiences. The same day, the encrypted Dev 2 branch advances from <code>1.60.1.69328</code> to <code>1.60.1.69407</code> (credited to dataminer Algalon).</li>
        <li><time>Aug 27 2026</time> Official WoW Armory adds support for Classic game versions (flagged by Joardee), letting Blizzard's web stack distinguish Classic realms/characters.</li>
        <li><time>Aug 28-29 2026</time> Three encrypted builds in ~25 hours: Dev 2 <code>69407→69555</code>, Dev 5 <code>69439→69606</code>, Dev 2 <code>69555→69609</code> — parallel 1.60.0/1.60.1 activity (Algalon/Ghostopheles tracker; Stiven notes possible BlizzCon show-realm prep).</li>
        <li><time>Sep 1 2026</time> wowdev2 advances to <code>1.60.1.69638</code>.</li>
        <li><time>Sep 5 2026</time> Dev 2 advances further; Dev 5 also receives a new build.</li>
        <li><time>Sep 12 2026</time> <strong>BlizzCon reveal: World of Warcraft: Forever.</strong> Beta September 17, launch November 4, first new raids December 9. The dev branch bounces to <code>1.60.1.69800</code> over reveal weekend then settles on <code>1.60.0.69818</code>.</li>
    </ul>
